-- Flex admission agreements: link each mention of the Yalla Family Handbook to the handbook in the Family Portal.
--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE "form_versions" SET "body" = 'Please read this agreement carefully. Add your initials where asked, then print your name and sign at the end. Once signed, it stays on file for one year, so you won’t be asked to sign it again before then.', "fields" = '[{"id": "intro", "type": "info", "text": "**Yalla Flex Admission Agreement · Seedlings (4 – 12 months) · 2026–2027**\n\nThis agreement is between Yalla Childcare LLC, doing business as Yalla Coworking & Childcare (“Yalla”), and the parent or caregiver signing below (the “Parent/Caregiver”), for the child named on this agreement (the “Child”). It covers every Yalla Flex session the Child attends for one (1) year from the date it is signed (the “Effective Date”). A new agreement must be signed before booking further Flex sessions when the Child moves to another Flex cohort or one year after signing, whichever comes first.\n\nThis agreement is a binding contract enforceable under the laws of the State of California. By signing, the Parent/Caregiver confirms they have read and accept these terms."}, {"id": "s1", "type": "heading", "text": "1. Overview"}, {"id": "s1-body", "type": "info", "text": "Yalla Coworking & Childcare is a license-exempt early childhood program operated at **408 Nutmeg Street, San Diego, CA 92103**, in accordance with California Health and Safety Code §1596.792. Yalla is directed and managed by a team of qualified administrators and early childhood educators committed to high-quality, developmentally appropriate care and enrichment for young children. The program supports children’s social, emotional, cognitive and physical development through play, inquiry-based learning and nurturing supervision.\n\nThis agreement applies to **Yalla Flex**, which lets children attend on an as-needed basis, without a recurring weekly or monthly schedule, when a spot is open in their age group. In this agreement, “childcare” means non-medical supervision and early learning experiences provided while the Child is on site."}, {"id": "s2", "type": "heading", "text": "2. Program hours and booking"}, {"id": "s2-body", "type": "info", "text": "Yalla Flex is available Monday through Friday, subject to availability:\n\n- **Full day:** 8:30 AM – 4:30 PM\n- **Half day:** 8:30 AM – 12:00 PM\n\nFlex sessions are booked online through the Yalla website or the Family Portal. A spot is available only when there is an opening in the Child’s age group; open days are shown on the booking calendar. Because our cohorts need time to prepare for each child, booking for a given day closes at 8:00 AM that morning. Yalla is closed, and Flex is not available, on the closure days listed on Yalla’s cohort year calendar.\n\nEarly Bird care (8:00–8:30 AM) is for children 12 months and older, so it is not available to the Seedlings cohort."}, {"id": "s3", "type": "heading", "text": "3. Rates, reservations and payment"}, {"id": "s3-body", "type": "info", "text": "**Seedlings (4 – 12 months) Flex rates**\n\n- **Full day (8:30 AM – 4:30 PM):** $180 per day\n- **Half day (8:30 AM – 12:00 PM):** $90 per day\n\nFlex rates include access to Yalla’s coworking space and amenities for the Parent/Caregiver, and snacks (for children eating solid foods), materials and participation in all programming offered during the Child’s booked hours. When siblings attend the same program on the same day, each additional child receives a 10% sibling discount, applied automatically at checkout.\n\nAll Flex sessions must be booked in advance and are paid in full at the time of booking. A session is reserved for the Child once payment is complete. The Parent/Caregiver may book one day at a time or several days at once; dates that have not been booked and paid for are not held, and availability may change.\n\nPrior use of Flex does not secure or prioritize future availability. Priority for cohort spaces is always given to Club Yalla members."}, {"id": "init-rates", "type": "initials", "label": "I have read and agree to Section 3: Flex rates, reservations and payment.", "required": true}, {"id": "s4", "type": "heading", "text": "4. Cancellations, absences and credits"}, {"id": "s4-body", "type": "info", "text": "When the Parent/Caregiver cancels a Flex session at least 24 hours before it begins, the amount paid is returned to the family’s Yalla Wallet as a credit. Credits can be used toward future Yalla bookings for up to 24 months from the date they are issued, have no cash value and are not refunded or transferred, except where required by law. Cancellations made less than 24 hours before a session, and no-shows, are not eligible for credit.\n\nIllness and other extenuating circumstances may be exempt from the 24-hour requirement; please contact Yalla as soon as possible. Cancel through the Family Portal, call 619.775.4008 or email hello@yallaspacesd.com.\n\nRepeated no-shows or cancellations without timely communication may result in the temporary suspension of Flex booking."}, {"id": "s5", "type": "heading", "text": "5. Child illness policy"}, {"id": "s5-body", "type": "info", "text": "The Parent/Caregiver agrees to follow Yalla’s [Illness Policy](/portal/illness-policy), available in the Family Portal. If the Child shows signs or symptoms of illness described in the policy, the Child will be separated from the group and supervised by Yalla staff until the Parent/Caregiver or another authorized adult collects the Child.\n\nThe Child will also be sent home when Yalla believes, in its sole judgment, that the Child’s condition poses a threat to the health or safety of the Child, other children or staff. Because the Parent/Caregiver remains on site during Flex sessions, **the Parent/Caregiver must collect the Child within twenty (20) minutes of being notified of the Child’s illness.** After twenty minutes, the Parent/Caregiver will be charged the actual cost of any additional expenses related to isolated care.\n\nIf the Child is sent home because of illness, the rest of that session is treated as an absence under Section 4.\n\nThe Child should be symptom-free for 24 hours before returning to care. Knowingly bringing a sick child to Yalla is a serious matter; repeated instances may result in the permanent end of Flex booking as described in Section 6. By signing this agreement, the Parent/Caregiver accepts responsibility for following the Illness Policy to protect the health and safety of all children in the program."}, {"id": "s6", "type": "heading", "text": "6. Ending Flex care"}, {"id": "s6-body", "type": "info", "text": "Yalla may end the Child’s participation in Yalla Flex **effective immediately** if any of the following occur:\n\n- In the sole discretion of Yalla’s leadership team, the behavior of the Child or the Parent/Caregiver presents a significant risk to the physical or emotional well-being of Yalla staff or anyone else on the premises, and that risk cannot be reasonably resolved through restorative communication.\n- Any amount owed to Yalla (for example, a late departure fee) is not paid within 10 days after it is due.\n- The Child is collected late more than three times in any thirty-day period without advance notice to Yalla.\n- The Child’s immunization record is not brought into compliance with California’s childcare immunization requirements within 21 days of the due date.\n\n*In compliance with California Health and Safety Code Sections 120325–120375, any child attending a private or public elementary or secondary school, childcare or preschool facility, day nursery, nursery school, family day care home or development center in California must be fully immunized before entry. Childcare providers are required to enforce immunization requirements, maintain immunization records and submit reports.*\n\n**Yalla also reserves the right to suspend or permanently end Flex booking at any time for any of the following reasons:**\n\n- Repeated failure to follow Yalla’s policies\n- Non-payment or repeated late payment of amounts owed\n- Behavior deemed unsafe or harmful by Yalla’s leadership\n- Repeated late departures\n- Missing required immunization documentation\n\nThese decisions are made at Yalla’s sole discretion to preserve the safety and integrity of the program."}, {"id": "s7", "type": "heading", "text": "7. Availability"}, {"id": "s7-body", "type": "info", "text": "Flex care can be booked at any time during the cohort year; however, availability is not guaranteed. Many of our cohorts are at or near capacity, and Flex is available only when there is an opening in the Child’s age group. Signing this agreement does not guarantee space on any particular day."}, {"id": "s8", "type": "heading", "text": "8. Arrival, departure and releasing children"}, {"id": "s8-body", "type": "info", "text": "Yalla will release the Child only to:\n\n- The Parent/Caregiver\n- An adult the Parent/Caregiver has authorized in writing in advance, listed in the family’s profile; or\n- Police or child welfare workers with proper authorization.\n\n**Yalla will never release the Child to anyone under the age of 18.**\n\nThe Parent/Caregiver or an authorized adult must check the Child in and sign the Child out at Yalla’s lobby kiosk at arrival and departure **every day**. The Child may never be taken from Yalla without first notifying the leadership team or the lead educarer or guide on duty in the Child’s cohort. Anyone other than the Parent/Caregiver who collects the Child must show a driver’s license or other valid photo identification.\n\nPlease plan to collect the Child by the end of the booked session. After a five-minute grace period, a late departure fee of $10 is charged for each additional ten minutes, or portion of ten minutes."}, {"id": "s9", "type": "heading", "text": "9. Educarers, guides and substitute care"}, {"id": "s9-body", "type": "info", "text": "The Child’s lead and supporting educarers and guides provide the vast majority of care and set the daily rhythm for the group. All caregivers are CPR and First Aid certified and have completed a LiveScan background check. Under Yalla’s own program requirements, caregivers also hold relevant advanced degrees and certifications.\n\nThere will be times when a cohort’s primary caregivers are attending professional development, out sick or away for personal matters. When the lead caregiver is absent, a supporting caregiver steps in as lead. A highly qualified substitute who spends time with the children at least once a month is available if both the lead and supporting caregivers are absent, so the program does not have to close.\n\nYalla is committed to hiring supporting caregivers and substitutes who are highly qualified and compensated well above industry standards for these roles. The Parent/Caregiver will be told of any change to the normal daily rhythm, including a change in the primary caregiver.\n\nAdult-to-child ratios are maintained throughout each program day at no more than 1:4 for children under 20 months, 1:6 for children 20 to 35 months, and 1:8 for children 3 years and older. The Seedlings cohort (4 – 12 months) is cared for at a ratio of no more than 1:4."}, {"id": "s10", "type": "heading", "text": "10. Staff qualifications, legal exemption status and onsite parent requirement"}, {"id": "s10-body", "type": "info", "text": "The Parent/Caregiver acknowledges that **Yalla is a license-exempt program** operating in accordance with **California Health and Safety Code §1596.792**. As a condition of this exemption, the Parent/Caregiver agrees to **remain physically present on Yalla’s premises at all times during the Child’s Flex session**. This exemption depends on the Child’s parent or legal guardian being on site and immediately available to provide care if needed, as defined by California law.\n\nYalla is deeply committed to the safety, development and well-being of every child, and **voluntarily follows the staff qualifications, safety standards and best practices in Title 22, Division 12, Chapter 1 of the California Code of Regulations**, including:\n\n- **§101216** – Personnel Requirements\n- **§101216.1** – Teacher Qualifications\n- **§101216.2** – Teacher Aide Qualifications\n- **§101216.3** – Teacher-Child Ratios\n- **§101215.1** – Director Qualifications\n- **§101170** – Criminal Record Clearance\n- **Health and Safety Code §1596.866** – Pediatric CPR/First Aid Training\n\nThis means that:\n\n- All Yalla staff are at least 18 years old, have the physical and mental capacity to care for children, and are trained in areas such as health, safety and child development.\n- Caregivers meet or exceed the education and experience qualifications in §101216.1, and aides meet the criteria in §101216.2.\n- Caregiver-to-child ratios meet or exceed those required of licensed programs, ensuring appropriate supervision and individual care.\n- Yalla’s director holds the professional qualifications needed to oversee early childhood programs, consistent with §101215.1.\n- All staff and volunteers complete **criminal background clearance** in compliance with §101170.\n- At least one adult with current **pediatric CPR and First Aid certification** is always on site, per HSC §1596.866.\n\nYalla also **maintains the standard documentation** and internal records required in licensed settings, including staff health screenings, immunizations and mandated reporter training records.\n\nThe Parent/Caregiver understands that **not remaining on site** may result in the **immediate end of Flex care** and may **jeopardize the program’s lawful exemption status** under California Health and Safety Code §1596.792."}, {"id": "init-onsite", "type": "initials", "label": "I have read and agree to Section 10, including that I will remain on Yalla’s premises for the whole of every Flex session.", "required": true}, {"id": "s11", "type": "heading", "text": "11. Family Handbook"}, {"id": "s11-body", "type": "info", "text": "On behalf of themselves and the Child, the Parent/Caregiver agrees to follow Yalla’s policies, rules and regulations, as Yalla may update them, including those in the [Yalla Family Handbook](/portal/handbook), available in the Family Portal. By entering into this agreement, the Parent/Caregiver agrees to accept and abide by Yalla’s philosophy, rules, regulations, policies, procedures and standards expressed or implied in the Family Handbook or other written Yalla policies."}, {"id": "init-handbook", "type": "initials", "label": "I have read and agree to Section 11: Yalla’s Family Handbook and policies.", "required": true}, {"id": "s12", "type": "heading", "text": "12. Parental consent and indemnity"}, {"id": "s12-body", "type": "info", "text": "The Parent/Caregiver gives permission for the Child to take part in all Yalla programming, including developmentally appropriate experiences and daily caregiving. The Parent/Caregiver shall indemnify, defend, release and hold harmless Yalla from and against any and all claims, damages, expenses and other liabilities or injuries arising out of the Child’s participation in program activities, excluding only liabilities or injuries caused by the sole gross negligence of Yalla."}, {"id": "s13", "type": "heading", "text": "13. Force majeure"}, {"id": "s13-body", "type": "info", "text": "Yalla’s failure to perform under this agreement is excused to the extent it is caused, in whole or in part, by events beyond Yalla’s control, including without limitation acts of God, disease, epidemic, pandemic, quarantine, governmental actions, terrorism or threats of terrorism, fire, flood, earthquake, storm, explosion, lightning, power surges or failures, the elements, civil disturbances, strikes or labor disputes, failures of transportation facilities, or any similar unforeseen event that makes performance commercially impracticable, illegal or impossible (a “Force Majeure Event”).\n\nThe parties agree that if a Force Majeure Event occurs, Yalla is relieved from performance under this agreement whether or not the event was foreseeable when this agreement was signed. Within a reasonable time after a Force Majeure Event first occurs, Yalla will notify the Parent/Caregiver by email or other written correspondence. Yalla may suspend childcare and related activities, or take other measures in response, with as little as one hour’s notice, including ending the cohort year, as Yalla considers necessary."}, {"id": "s14", "type": "heading", "text": "14. Duty to report child abuse"}, {"id": "s14-body", "type": "info", "text": "Yalla staff are mandated reporters of suspected child abuse under California Penal Code §11166. Staff who, in their professional capacity or within the scope of their employment, know of or observe a child whom they know or reasonably suspect has been the victim of child abuse have a legal duty to report it to a child protective agency. Staff who know of or reasonably suspect that mental suffering has been inflicted on a child, or that a child’s emotional well-being is endangered in any other way, must also report it to a child protective agency."}, {"id": "s15", "type": "heading", "text": "15. Food"}, {"id": "s15-body", "type": "info", "text": "The Parent/Caregiver provides all food for the Child each day, following the guidelines in the [Yalla Family Handbook](/portal/handbook).\n\n- The Child must arrive each day with all required food, premade bottles, and formula or expressed breast milk, in sufficient quantities for the whole session. All bottles and food containers must be clearly labeled with the Child’s full name and the date, and stored and transported following the safe-handling practices in the [Family Handbook](/portal/handbook#breast-milk). Staff follow each child’s individual feeding schedule as provided by the Parent/Caregiver.\n- A Parent/Caregiver who chooses to breastfeed during the day is responsible for coordinating directly with the Child’s caregiving team to set a consistent, respectful feeding schedule.\n- Once the Child eats solid foods, food must be fully prepared in advance, cut into safe, age-appropriate portions, and stored with ice packs or in a thermos as needed. Yalla does not prepare or modify meals on site; each cohort space has a microwave for **optional meal reheating**, and the Parent/Caregiver may tell the Child’s caregiver whether they would like meals reheated.\n- Yalla provides snacks only to children who eat solid foods.\n\nIf the Child arrives without enough food, or with food that does not follow Yalla’s safety or allergy guidelines, Yalla may ask the Parent/Caregiver to provide appropriate food. If food is missing or unsuitable and it is not resolved promptly, the Child may be sent home for the day. The Parent/Caregiver is responsible for making sure the Child’s food meets all safety, allergy and developmental requirements, to protect the health and well-being of every child in care. Yalla is a nut-free environment."}, {"id": "s16", "type": "heading", "text": "16. Non-discrimination"}, {"id": "s16-body", "type": "info", "text": "At Yalla Coworking & Childcare, we are deeply committed to a welcoming, inclusive and respectful environment for every family. We embrace children and caregivers of every race, ethnicity, national origin, family structure, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion and background.\n\nWe do not tolerate discrimination of any kind within our community, and all families are expected to uphold these values. Discriminatory behavior, or conduct that undermines the inclusive nature of our program, may result in the end of Flex care under Section 6. We believe diversity strengthens our community, and we are proud to welcome families of all kinds."}, {"id": "s17", "type": "heading", "text": "17. Waiver"}, {"id": "s17-body", "type": "info", "text": "No right under this agreement is waived (lost) merely by delaying or failing to exercise it. Consent to one act is not consent to any other or later act. Any waiver of a default under this agreement must be in writing and is not a waiver of any other default concerning the same or any other provision of this agreement."}, {"id": "s18", "type": "heading", "text": "18. Good faith"}, {"id": "s18-body", "type": "info", "text": "At Yalla, we believe in a partnership built on mutual trust and respect. Yalla and the Parent/Caregiver each agree to act in good faith and with mutual respect for the duration of this agreement, including:\n\n- **Honesty and transparency:** communicating honestly and openly about all matters related to the Child’s care, health and well-being.\n- **Timely communication:** sharing any concerns, issues or changes in circumstances that may affect the Child’s care promptly, so they can be resolved quickly with minimal disruption.\n- **Respectful interactions:** conducting all interactions between Yalla, the Parent/Caregiver and other members of the Yalla community with mutual respect and consideration.\n- **Cooperation and collaboration:** working together to address any issues or challenges, seeking solutions in the best interest of the Child.\n- **Commitment to these terms:** following the terms of this agreement, understanding that its success depends on the reliability and integrity of both Yalla and the Parent/Caregiver.\n\nBy signing, both parties commit to acting in good faith to support a positive environment for the Child’s growth and development."}, {"id": "s19", "type": "heading", "text": "19. Governing law"}, {"id": "s19-body", "type": "info", "text": "This agreement is governed by the laws of the State of California, without regard to conflict-of-laws principles. Each party irrevocably consents to the exclusive personal jurisdiction and venue of the federal and state courts located in the County of San Diego, California, for any matter arising out of or relating to this agreement."}, {"id": "sign", "type": "heading", "text": "Signatures"}, {"id": "sign-body", "type": "info", "text": "**The undersigned have read and understand this agreement.**\n\nThis agreement and the [Yalla Family Handbook](/portal/handbook) (available in the Family Portal) set out all of Yalla’s obligations; there are no other implied obligations. Any changes to this agreement must be in writing and signed by both parties.\n\nYalla accepts this agreement on the date it is signed below. Accepted for Yalla Childcare LLC by Elizabeth Coburn, Managing Partner."}, {"id": "read-understood", "type": "agree", "label": "I am the child’s parent or legal guardian and have read and agree to the Seedlings Flex admission agreement. This agreement applies to any Seedlings Flex sessions I book and does not require a commitment to future care. A new agreement is required only when my child moves to another Flex cohort or one year after signing, whichever comes first.", "required": true}, {"id": "signature", "type": "signature", "label": "Parent/Caregiver signature"}]'::jsonb, "content_hash" = '6f902e52d8f749416ee0b2b17270a14e7700692de5e3c5a39c144c7bff23d18c' WHERE "id" = 'flex-agreement-seedlings-v1' AND "body" = 'Please read this agreement carefully. Add your initials where asked, then print your name and sign at the end. Once signed, it stays on file for one year, so you won’t be asked to sign it again before then.' AND "fields"::text LIKE '%Yalla’s [Illness Policy](/portal/illness-policy), available in the Family Portal%' AND "fields"::text NOT LIKE '%(/portal/handbook%' AND NOT "fields" @> '[{"id": "parent-name"}]'::jsonb;
--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE "form_versions" SET "body" = 'Please read this agreement carefully. Add your initials where asked, then print your name and sign at the end. Once signed, it stays on file for one year, so you won’t be asked to sign it again before then.', "fields" = '[{"id": "intro", "type": "info", "text": "**Yalla Flex Admission Agreement · Saplings (12 – 20 months) · 2026–2027**\n\nThis agreement is between Yalla Childcare LLC, doing business as Yalla Coworking & Childcare (“Yalla”), and the parent or caregiver signing below (the “Parent/Caregiver”), for the child named on this agreement (the “Child”). It covers every Yalla Flex session the Child attends for one (1) year from the date it is signed (the “Effective Date”). A new agreement must be signed before booking further Flex sessions when the Child moves to another Flex cohort or one year after signing, whichever comes first.\n\nThis agreement is a binding contract enforceable under the laws of the State of California. By signing, the Parent/Caregiver confirms they have read and accept these terms."}, {"id": "s1", "type": "heading", "text": "1. Overview"}, {"id": "s1-body", "type": "info", "text": "Yalla Coworking & Childcare is a license-exempt early childhood program operated at **408 Nutmeg Street, San Diego, CA 92103**, in accordance with California Health and Safety Code §1596.792. Yalla is directed and managed by a team of qualified administrators and early childhood educators committed to high-quality, developmentally appropriate care and enrichment for young children. The program supports children’s social, emotional, cognitive and physical development through play, inquiry-based learning and nurturing supervision.\n\nThis agreement applies to **Yalla Flex**, which lets children attend on an as-needed basis, without a recurring weekly or monthly schedule, when a spot is open in their age group. In this agreement, “childcare” means non-medical supervision and early learning experiences provided while the Child is on site."}, {"id": "s2", "type": "heading", "text": "2. Program hours and booking"}, {"id": "s2-body", "type": "info", "text": "Yalla Flex is available Monday through Friday, subject to availability:\n\n- **Full day:** 8:30 AM – 4:30 PM\n- **Half day:** 8:30 AM – 12:00 PM\n\nFlex sessions are booked online through the Yalla website or the Family Portal. A spot is available only when there is an opening in the Child’s age group; open days are shown on the booking calendar. Because our cohorts need time to prepare for each child, booking for a given day closes at 8:00 AM that morning. Yalla is closed, and Flex is not available, on the closure days listed on Yalla’s cohort year calendar.\n\nEarly Bird care is offered from 8:00–8:30 AM for children 12 months and older, at $16 per day, on days when Yalla has Early Bird space available. Early Bird space is limited and is shown at booking when it is available; an open Flex session does not guarantee an Early Bird space."}, {"id": "s3", "type": "heading", "text": "3. Rates, reservations and payment"}, {"id": "s3-body", "type": "info", "text": "**Saplings (12 – 20 months) Flex rates**\n\n- **Full day (8:30 AM – 4:30 PM):** $160 per day\n- **Half day (8:30 AM – 12:00 PM):** $80 per day\n\nFlex rates include access to Yalla’s coworking space and amenities for the Parent/Caregiver, and snacks (for children eating solid foods), materials and participation in all programming offered during the Child’s booked hours. When siblings attend the same program on the same day, each additional child receives a 10% sibling discount, applied automatically at checkout.\n\nAll Flex sessions must be booked in advance and are paid in full at the time of booking. A session is reserved for the Child once payment is complete. The Parent/Caregiver may book one day at a time or several days at once; dates that have not been booked and paid for are not held, and availability may change.\n\nPrior use of Flex does not secure or prioritize future availability. Priority for cohort spaces is always given to Club Yalla members."}, {"id": "init-rates", "type": "initials", "label": "I have read and agree to Section 3: Flex rates, reservations and payment.", "required": true}, {"id": "s4", "type": "heading", "text": "4. Cancellations, absences and credits"}, {"id": "s4-body", "type": "info", "text": "When the Parent/Caregiver cancels a Flex session at least 24 hours before it begins, the amount paid is returned to the family’s Yalla Wallet as a credit. Credits can be used toward future Yalla bookings for up to 24 months from the date they are issued, have no cash value and are not refunded or transferred, except where required by law. Cancellations made less than 24 hours before a session, and no-shows, are not eligible for credit.\n\nIllness and other extenuating circumstances may be exempt from the 24-hour requirement; please contact Yalla as soon as possible. Cancel through the Family Portal, call 619.775.4008 or email hello@yallaspacesd.com.\n\nRepeated no-shows or cancellations without timely communication may result in the temporary suspension of Flex booking."}, {"id": "s5", "type": "heading", "text": "5. Child illness policy"}, {"id": "s5-body", "type": "info", "text": "The Parent/Caregiver agrees to follow Yalla’s [Illness Policy](/portal/illness-policy), available in the Family Portal. If the Child shows signs or symptoms of illness described in the policy, the Child will be separated from the group and supervised by Yalla staff until the Parent/Caregiver or another authorized adult collects the Child.\n\nThe Child will also be sent home when Yalla believes, in its sole judgment, that the Child’s condition poses a threat to the health or safety of the Child, other children or staff. Because the Parent/Caregiver remains on site during Flex sessions, **the Parent/Caregiver must collect the Child within twenty (20) minutes of being notified of the Child’s illness.** After twenty minutes, the Parent/Caregiver will be charged the actual cost of any additional expenses related to isolated care.\n\nIf the Child is sent home because of illness, the rest of that session is treated as an absence under Section 4.\n\nThe Child should be symptom-free for 24 hours before returning to care. Knowingly bringing a sick child to Yalla is a serious matter; repeated instances may result in the permanent end of Flex booking as described in Section 6. By signing this agreement, the Parent/Caregiver accepts responsibility for following the Illness Policy to protect the health and safety of all children in the program."}, {"id": "s6", "type": "heading", "text": "6. Ending Flex care"}, {"id": "s6-body", "type": "info", "text": "Yalla may end the Child’s participation in Yalla Flex **effective immediately** if any of the following occur:\n\n- In the sole discretion of Yalla’s leadership team, the behavior of the Child or the Parent/Caregiver presents a significant risk to the physical or emotional well-being of Yalla staff or anyone else on the premises, and that risk cannot be reasonably resolved through restorative communication.\n- Any amount owed to Yalla (for example, a late departure fee) is not paid within 10 days after it is due.\n- The Child is collected late more than three times in any thirty-day period without advance notice to Yalla.\n- The Child’s immunization record is not brought into compliance with California’s childcare immunization requirements within 21 days of the due date.\n\n*In compliance with California Health and Safety Code Sections 120325–120375, any child attending a private or public elementary or secondary school, childcare or preschool facility, day nursery, nursery school, family day care home or development center in California must be fully immunized before entry. Childcare providers are required to enforce immunization requirements, maintain immunization records and submit reports.*\n\n**Yalla also reserves the right to suspend or permanently end Flex booking at any time for any of the following reasons:**\n\n- Repeated failure to follow Yalla’s policies\n- Non-payment or repeated late payment of amounts owed\n- Behavior deemed unsafe or harmful by Yalla’s leadership\n- Repeated late departures\n- Missing required immunization documentation\n\nThese decisions are made at Yalla’s sole discretion to preserve the safety and integrity of the program."}, {"id": "s7", "type": "heading", "text": "7. Availability"}, {"id": "s7-body", "type": "info", "text": "Flex care can be booked at any time during the cohort year; however, availability is not guaranteed. Many of our cohorts are at or near capacity, and Flex is available only when there is an opening in the Child’s age group. Signing this agreement does not guarantee space on any particular day."}, {"id": "s8", "type": "heading", "text": "8. Arrival, departure and releasing children"}, {"id": "s8-body", "type": "info", "text": "Yalla will release the Child only to:\n\n- The Parent/Caregiver\n- An adult the Parent/Caregiver has authorized in writing in advance, listed in the family’s profile; or\n- Police or child welfare workers with proper authorization.\n\n**Yalla will never release the Child to anyone under the age of 18.**\n\nThe Parent/Caregiver or an authorized adult must check the Child in and sign the Child out at Yalla’s lobby kiosk at arrival and departure **every day**. The Child may never be taken from Yalla without first notifying the leadership team or the lead educarer or guide on duty in the Child’s cohort. Anyone other than the Parent/Caregiver who collects the Child must show a driver’s license or other valid photo identification.\n\nPlease plan to collect the Child by the end of the booked session. After a five-minute grace period, a late departure fee of $10 is charged for each additional ten minutes, or portion of ten minutes."}, {"id": "s9", "type": "heading", "text": "9. Educarers, guides and substitute care"}, {"id": "s9-body", "type": "info", "text": "The Child’s lead and supporting educarers and guides provide the vast majority of care and set the daily rhythm for the group. All caregivers are CPR and First Aid certified and have completed a LiveScan background check. Under Yalla’s own program requirements, caregivers also hold relevant advanced degrees and certifications.\n\nThere will be times when a cohort’s primary caregivers are attending professional development, out sick or away for personal matters. When the lead caregiver is absent, a supporting caregiver steps in as lead. A highly qualified substitute who spends time with the children at least once a month is available if both the lead and supporting caregivers are absent, so the program does not have to close.\n\nYalla is committed to hiring supporting caregivers and substitutes who are highly qualified and compensated well above industry standards for these roles. The Parent/Caregiver will be told of any change to the normal daily rhythm, including a change in the primary caregiver.\n\nAdult-to-child ratios are maintained throughout each program day at no more than 1:4 for children under 20 months, 1:6 for children 20 to 35 months, and 1:8 for children 3 years and older. The Saplings cohort (12 – 20 months) is cared for at a ratio of no more than 1:4."}, {"id": "s10", "type": "heading", "text": "10. Staff qualifications, legal exemption status and onsite parent requirement"}, {"id": "s10-body", "type": "info", "text": "The Parent/Caregiver acknowledges that **Yalla is a license-exempt program** operating in accordance with **California Health and Safety Code §1596.792**. As a condition of this exemption, the Parent/Caregiver agrees to **remain physically present on Yalla’s premises at all times during the Child’s Flex session**. This exemption depends on the Child’s parent or legal guardian being on site and immediately available to provide care if needed, as defined by California law.\n\nYalla is deeply committed to the safety, development and well-being of every child, and **voluntarily follows the staff qualifications, safety standards and best practices in Title 22, Division 12, Chapter 1 of the California Code of Regulations**, including:\n\n- **§101216** – Personnel Requirements\n- **§101216.1** – Teacher Qualifications\n- **§101216.2** – Teacher Aide Qualifications\n- **§101216.3** – Teacher-Child Ratios\n- **§101215.1** – Director Qualifications\n- **§101170** – Criminal Record Clearance\n- **Health and Safety Code §1596.866** – Pediatric CPR/First Aid Training\n\nThis means that:\n\n- All Yalla staff are at least 18 years old, have the physical and mental capacity to care for children, and are trained in areas such as health, safety and child development.\n- Caregivers meet or exceed the education and experience qualifications in §101216.1, and aides meet the criteria in §101216.2.\n- Caregiver-to-child ratios meet or exceed those required of licensed programs, ensuring appropriate supervision and individual care.\n- Yalla’s director holds the professional qualifications needed to oversee early childhood programs, consistent with §101215.1.\n- All staff and volunteers complete **criminal background clearance** in compliance with §101170.\n- At least one adult with current **pediatric CPR and First Aid certification** is always on site, per HSC §1596.866.\n\nYalla also **maintains the standard documentation** and internal records required in licensed settings, including staff health screenings, immunizations and mandated reporter training records.\n\nThe Parent/Caregiver understands that **not remaining on site** may result in the **immediate end of Flex care** and may **jeopardize the program’s lawful exemption status** under California Health and Safety Code §1596.792."}, {"id": "init-onsite", "type": "initials", "label": "I have read and agree to Section 10, including that I will remain on Yalla’s premises for the whole of every Flex session.", "required": true}, {"id": "s11", "type": "heading", "text": "11. Family Handbook"}, {"id": "s11-body", "type": "info", "text": "On behalf of themselves and the Child, the Parent/Caregiver agrees to follow Yalla’s policies, rules and regulations, as Yalla may update them, including those in the [Yalla Family Handbook](/portal/handbook), available in the Family Portal. By entering into this agreement, the Parent/Caregiver agrees to accept and abide by Yalla’s philosophy, rules, regulations, policies, procedures and standards expressed or implied in the Family Handbook or other written Yalla policies."}, {"id": "init-handbook", "type": "initials", "label": "I have read and agree to Section 11: Yalla’s Family Handbook and policies.", "required": true}, {"id": "s12", "type": "heading", "text": "12. Parental consent and indemnity"}, {"id": "s12-body", "type": "info", "text": "The Parent/Caregiver gives permission for the Child to take part in all Yalla programming, including developmentally appropriate experiences and daily caregiving. The Parent/Caregiver shall indemnify, defend, release and hold harmless Yalla from and against any and all claims, damages, expenses and other liabilities or injuries arising out of the Child’s participation in program activities, excluding only liabilities or injuries caused by the sole gross negligence of Yalla."}, {"id": "s13", "type": "heading", "text": "13. Force majeure"}, {"id": "s13-body", "type": "info", "text": "Yalla’s failure to perform under this agreement is excused to the extent it is caused, in whole or in part, by events beyond Yalla’s control, including without limitation acts of God, disease, epidemic, pandemic, quarantine, governmental actions, terrorism or threats of terrorism, fire, flood, earthquake, storm, explosion, lightning, power surges or failures, the elements, civil disturbances, strikes or labor disputes, failures of transportation facilities, or any similar unforeseen event that makes performance commercially impracticable, illegal or impossible (a “Force Majeure Event”).\n\nThe parties agree that if a Force Majeure Event occurs, Yalla is relieved from performance under this agreement whether or not the event was foreseeable when this agreement was signed. Within a reasonable time after a Force Majeure Event first occurs, Yalla will notify the Parent/Caregiver by email or other written correspondence. Yalla may suspend childcare and related activities, or take other measures in response, with as little as one hour’s notice, including ending the cohort year, as Yalla considers necessary."}, {"id": "s14", "type": "heading", "text": "14. Duty to report child abuse"}, {"id": "s14-body", "type": "info", "text": "Yalla staff are mandated reporters of suspected child abuse under California Penal Code §11166. Staff who, in their professional capacity or within the scope of their employment, know of or observe a child whom they know or reasonably suspect has been the victim of child abuse have a legal duty to report it to a child protective agency. Staff who know of or reasonably suspect that mental suffering has been inflicted on a child, or that a child’s emotional well-being is endangered in any other way, must also report it to a child protective agency."}, {"id": "s15", "type": "heading", "text": "15. Food"}, {"id": "s15-body", "type": "info", "text": "The Parent/Caregiver provides all food for the Child each day, following the guidelines in the [Yalla Family Handbook](/portal/handbook).\n\n- If the Child still drinks from bottles, the Child must arrive with premade bottles and formula or expressed breast milk, in sufficient quantities for the whole session, clearly labeled with the Child’s full name and the date, and stored and transported following the safe-handling practices in the [Family Handbook](/portal/handbook#breast-milk). Staff follow the Child’s individual feeding schedule as provided by the Parent/Caregiver.\n- A Parent/Caregiver who chooses to breastfeed during the day is responsible for coordinating directly with the Child’s caregiving team to set a consistent, respectful feeding schedule.\n- Children who eat solid foods must bring a nutritious, ready-to-eat lunch each day that follows Yalla’s dietary restrictions, choking-prevention requirements and safe food preparation policies. Food must be fully prepared in advance, stored with ice packs or in a thermos, and cut into safe, age-appropriate portions. Yalla does not prepare or modify meals on site; each cohort space has a microwave for **optional meal reheating**, and the Parent/Caregiver may tell the Child’s caregiver whether they would like meals reheated.\n- Yalla provides snacks only to children who eat solid foods.\n\nIf the Child arrives without enough food, or with food that does not follow Yalla’s safety or allergy guidelines, Yalla may ask the Parent/Caregiver to provide appropriate food. If food is missing or unsuitable and it is not resolved promptly, the Child may be sent home for the day. The Parent/Caregiver is responsible for making sure the Child’s food meets all safety, allergy and developmental requirements, to protect the health and well-being of every child in care. Yalla is a nut-free environment."}, {"id": "s16", "type": "heading", "text": "16. Non-discrimination"}, {"id": "s16-body", "type": "info", "text": "At Yalla Coworking & Childcare, we are deeply committed to a welcoming, inclusive and respectful environment for every family. We embrace children and caregivers of every race, ethnicity, national origin, family structure, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion and background.\n\nWe do not tolerate discrimination of any kind within our community, and all families are expected to uphold these values. Discriminatory behavior, or conduct that undermines the inclusive nature of our program, may result in the end of Flex care under Section 6. We believe diversity strengthens our community, and we are proud to welcome families of all kinds."}, {"id": "s17", "type": "heading", "text": "17. Waiver"}, {"id": "s17-body", "type": "info", "text": "No right under this agreement is waived (lost) merely by delaying or failing to exercise it. Consent to one act is not consent to any other or later act. Any waiver of a default under this agreement must be in writing and is not a waiver of any other default concerning the same or any other provision of this agreement."}, {"id": "s18", "type": "heading", "text": "18. Good faith"}, {"id": "s18-body", "type": "info", "text": "At Yalla, we believe in a partnership built on mutual trust and respect. Yalla and the Parent/Caregiver each agree to act in good faith and with mutual respect for the duration of this agreement, including:\n\n- **Honesty and transparency:** communicating honestly and openly about all matters related to the Child’s care, health and well-being.\n- **Timely communication:** sharing any concerns, issues or changes in circumstances that may affect the Child’s care promptly, so they can be resolved quickly with minimal disruption.\n- **Respectful interactions:** conducting all interactions between Yalla, the Parent/Caregiver and other members of the Yalla community with mutual respect and consideration.\n- **Cooperation and collaboration:** working together to address any issues or challenges, seeking solutions in the best interest of the Child.\n- **Commitment to these terms:** following the terms of this agreement, understanding that its success depends on the reliability and integrity of both Yalla and the Parent/Caregiver.\n\nBy signing, both parties commit to acting in good faith to support a positive environment for the Child’s growth and development."}, {"id": "s19", "type": "heading", "text": "19. Governing law"}, {"id": "s19-body", "type": "info", "text": "This agreement is governed by the laws of the State of California, without regard to conflict-of-laws principles. Each party irrevocably consents to the exclusive personal jurisdiction and venue of the federal and state courts located in the County of San Diego, California, for any matter arising out of or relating to this agreement."}, {"id": "sign", "type": "heading", "text": "Signatures"}, {"id": "sign-body", "type": "info", "text": "**The undersigned have read and understand this agreement.**\n\nThis agreement and the [Yalla Family Handbook](/portal/handbook) (available in the Family Portal) set out all of Yalla’s obligations; there are no other implied obligations. Any changes to this agreement must be in writing and signed by both parties.\n\nYalla accepts this agreement on the date it is signed below. Accepted for Yalla Childcare LLC by Elizabeth Coburn, Managing Partner."}, {"id": "read-understood", "type": "agree", "label": "I am the child’s parent or legal guardian and have read and agree to the Saplings Flex admission agreement. This agreement applies to any Saplings Flex sessions I book and does not require a commitment to future care. A new agreement is required only when my child moves to another Flex cohort or one year after signing, whichever comes first.", "required": true}, {"id": "signature", "type": "signature", "label": "Parent/Caregiver signature"}]'::jsonb, "content_hash" = '744b61bd8b1f95d7d8d654c8d81f2bec34b364fbc3c941e8de8a6dfe31193692' WHERE "id" = 'flex-agreement-saplings-v1' AND "body" = 'Please read this agreement carefully. Add your initials where asked, then print your name and sign at the end. Once signed, it stays on file for one year, so you won’t be asked to sign it again before then.' AND "fields"::text LIKE '%Yalla’s [Illness Policy](/portal/illness-policy), available in the Family Portal%' AND "fields"::text NOT LIKE '%(/portal/handbook%' AND NOT "fields" @> '[{"id": "parent-name"}]'::jsonb;
--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE "form_versions" SET "body" = 'Please read this agreement carefully. Add your initials where asked, then print your name and sign at the end. Once signed, it stays on file for one year, so you won’t be asked to sign it again before then.', "fields" = '[{"id": "intro", "type": "info", "text": "**Yalla Flex Admission Agreement · Sprouts (20 – 35 months) · 2026–2027**\n\nThis agreement is between Yalla Childcare LLC, doing business as Yalla Coworking & Childcare (“Yalla”), and the parent or caregiver signing below (the “Parent/Caregiver”), for the child named on this agreement (the “Child”). It covers every Yalla Flex session the Child attends for one (1) year from the date it is signed (the “Effective Date”). A new agreement must be signed before booking further Flex sessions when the Child moves to another Flex cohort or one year after signing, whichever comes first.\n\nThis agreement is a binding contract enforceable under the laws of the State of California. By signing, the Parent/Caregiver confirms they have read and accept these terms."}, {"id": "s1", "type": "heading", "text": "1. Overview"}, {"id": "s1-body", "type": "info", "text": "Yalla Coworking & Childcare is a license-exempt early childhood program operated at **408 Nutmeg Street, San Diego, CA 92103**, in accordance with California Health and Safety Code §1596.792. Yalla is directed and managed by a team of qualified administrators and early childhood educators committed to high-quality, developmentally appropriate care and enrichment for young children. The program supports children’s social, emotional, cognitive and physical development through play, inquiry-based learning and nurturing supervision.\n\nThis agreement applies to **Yalla Flex**, which lets children attend on an as-needed basis, without a recurring weekly or monthly schedule, when a spot is open in their age group. In this agreement, “childcare” means non-medical supervision and early learning experiences provided while the Child is on site."}, {"id": "s2", "type": "heading", "text": "2. Program hours and booking"}, {"id": "s2-body", "type": "info", "text": "Yalla Flex is available Monday through Friday, subject to availability:\n\n- **Full day:** 8:30 AM – 4:30 PM\n- **Half day:** 8:30 AM – 12:00 PM\n\nFlex sessions are booked online through the Yalla website or the Family Portal. A spot is available only when there is an opening in the Child’s age group; open days are shown on the booking calendar. Because our cohorts need time to prepare for each child, booking for a given day closes at 8:00 AM that morning. Yalla is closed, and Flex is not available, on the closure days listed on Yalla’s cohort year calendar.\n\nEarly Bird care is offered from 8:00–8:30 AM for children 12 months and older, at $16 per day, on days when Yalla has Early Bird space available. Early Bird space is limited and is shown at booking when it is available; an open Flex session does not guarantee an Early Bird space."}, {"id": "s3", "type": "heading", "text": "3. Rates, reservations and payment"}, {"id": "s3-body", "type": "info", "text": "**Sprouts (20 – 35 months) Flex rates**\n\n- **Full day (8:30 AM – 4:30 PM):** $150 per day\n- **Half day (8:30 AM – 12:00 PM):** $75 per day\n\nFlex rates include access to Yalla’s coworking space and amenities for the Parent/Caregiver, and snacks (for children eating solid foods), materials and participation in all programming offered during the Child’s booked hours. When siblings attend the same program on the same day, each additional child receives a 10% sibling discount, applied automatically at checkout.\n\nAll Flex sessions must be booked in advance and are paid in full at the time of booking. A session is reserved for the Child once payment is complete. The Parent/Caregiver may book one day at a time or several days at once; dates that have not been booked and paid for are not held, and availability may change.\n\nPrior use of Flex does not secure or prioritize future availability. Priority for cohort spaces is always given to Club Yalla members."}, {"id": "init-rates", "type": "initials", "label": "I have read and agree to Section 3: Flex rates, reservations and payment.", "required": true}, {"id": "s4", "type": "heading", "text": "4. Cancellations, absences and credits"}, {"id": "s4-body", "type": "info", "text": "When the Parent/Caregiver cancels a Flex session at least 24 hours before it begins, the amount paid is returned to the family’s Yalla Wallet as a credit. Credits can be used toward future Yalla bookings for up to 24 months from the date they are issued, have no cash value and are not refunded or transferred, except where required by law. Cancellations made less than 24 hours before a session, and no-shows, are not eligible for credit.\n\nIllness and other extenuating circumstances may be exempt from the 24-hour requirement; please contact Yalla as soon as possible. Cancel through the Family Portal, call 619.775.4008 or email hello@yallaspacesd.com.\n\nRepeated no-shows or cancellations without timely communication may result in the temporary suspension of Flex booking."}, {"id": "s5", "type": "heading", "text": "5. Child illness policy"}, {"id": "s5-body", "type": "info", "text": "The Parent/Caregiver agrees to follow Yalla’s [Illness Policy](/portal/illness-policy), available in the Family Portal. If the Child shows signs or symptoms of illness described in the policy, the Child will be separated from the group and supervised by Yalla staff until the Parent/Caregiver or another authorized adult collects the Child.\n\nThe Child will also be sent home when Yalla believes, in its sole judgment, that the Child’s condition poses a threat to the health or safety of the Child, other children or staff. Because the Parent/Caregiver remains on site during Flex sessions, **the Parent/Caregiver must collect the Child within twenty (20) minutes of being notified of the Child’s illness.** After twenty minutes, the Parent/Caregiver will be charged the actual cost of any additional expenses related to isolated care.\n\nIf the Child is sent home because of illness, the rest of that session is treated as an absence under Section 4.\n\nThe Child should be symptom-free for 24 hours before returning to care. Knowingly bringing a sick child to Yalla is a serious matter; repeated instances may result in the permanent end of Flex booking as described in Section 6. By signing this agreement, the Parent/Caregiver accepts responsibility for following the Illness Policy to protect the health and safety of all children in the program."}, {"id": "s6", "type": "heading", "text": "6. Ending Flex care"}, {"id": "s6-body", "type": "info", "text": "Yalla may end the Child’s participation in Yalla Flex **effective immediately** if any of the following occur:\n\n- In the sole discretion of Yalla’s leadership team, the behavior of the Child or the Parent/Caregiver presents a significant risk to the physical or emotional well-being of Yalla staff or anyone else on the premises, and that risk cannot be reasonably resolved through restorative communication.\n- Any amount owed to Yalla (for example, a late departure fee) is not paid within 10 days after it is due.\n- The Child is collected late more than three times in any thirty-day period without advance notice to Yalla.\n- The Child’s immunization record is not brought into compliance with California’s childcare immunization requirements within 21 days of the due date.\n\n*In compliance with California Health and Safety Code Sections 120325–120375, any child attending a private or public elementary or secondary school, childcare or preschool facility, day nursery, nursery school, family day care home or development center in California must be fully immunized before entry. Childcare providers are required to enforce immunization requirements, maintain immunization records and submit reports.*\n\n**Yalla also reserves the right to suspend or permanently end Flex booking at any time for any of the following reasons:**\n\n- Repeated failure to follow Yalla’s policies\n- Non-payment or repeated late payment of amounts owed\n- Behavior deemed unsafe or harmful by Yalla’s leadership\n- Repeated late departures\n- Missing required immunization documentation\n\nThese decisions are made at Yalla’s sole discretion to preserve the safety and integrity of the program."}, {"id": "s7", "type": "heading", "text": "7. Availability"}, {"id": "s7-body", "type": "info", "text": "Flex care can be booked at any time during the cohort year; however, availability is not guaranteed. Many of our cohorts are at or near capacity, and Flex is available only when there is an opening in the Child’s age group. Signing this agreement does not guarantee space on any particular day."}, {"id": "s8", "type": "heading", "text": "8. Arrival, departure and releasing children"}, {"id": "s8-body", "type": "info", "text": "Yalla will release the Child only to:\n\n- The Parent/Caregiver\n- An adult the Parent/Caregiver has authorized in writing in advance, listed in the family’s profile; or\n- Police or child welfare workers with proper authorization.\n\n**Yalla will never release the Child to anyone under the age of 18.**\n\nThe Parent/Caregiver or an authorized adult must check the Child in and sign the Child out at Yalla’s lobby kiosk at arrival and departure **every day**. The Child may never be taken from Yalla without first notifying the leadership team or the lead educarer or guide on duty in the Child’s cohort. Anyone other than the Parent/Caregiver who collects the Child must show a driver’s license or other valid photo identification.\n\nPlease plan to collect the Child by the end of the booked session. After a five-minute grace period, a late departure fee of $10 is charged for each additional ten minutes, or portion of ten minutes."}, {"id": "s9", "type": "heading", "text": "9. Educarers, guides and substitute care"}, {"id": "s9-body", "type": "info", "text": "The Child’s lead and supporting educarers and guides provide the vast majority of care and set the daily rhythm for the group. All caregivers are CPR and First Aid certified and have completed a LiveScan background check. Under Yalla’s own program requirements, caregivers also hold relevant advanced degrees and certifications.\n\nThere will be times when a cohort’s primary caregivers are attending professional development, out sick or away for personal matters. When the lead caregiver is absent, a supporting caregiver steps in as lead. A highly qualified substitute who spends time with the children at least once a month is available if both the lead and supporting caregivers are absent, so the program does not have to close.\n\nYalla is committed to hiring supporting caregivers and substitutes who are highly qualified and compensated well above industry standards for these roles. The Parent/Caregiver will be told of any change to the normal daily rhythm, including a change in the primary caregiver.\n\nAdult-to-child ratios are maintained throughout each program day at no more than 1:4 for children under 20 months, 1:6 for children 20 to 35 months, and 1:8 for children 3 years and older. The Sprouts cohort (20 – 35 months) is cared for at a ratio of no more than 1:6."}, {"id": "s10", "type": "heading", "text": "10. Staff qualifications, legal exemption status and onsite parent requirement"}, {"id": "s10-body", "type": "info", "text": "The Parent/Caregiver acknowledges that **Yalla is a license-exempt program** operating in accordance with **California Health and Safety Code §1596.792**. As a condition of this exemption, the Parent/Caregiver agrees to **remain physically present on Yalla’s premises at all times during the Child’s Flex session**. This exemption depends on the Child’s parent or legal guardian being on site and immediately available to provide care if needed, as defined by California law.\n\nYalla is deeply committed to the safety, development and well-being of every child, and **voluntarily follows the staff qualifications, safety standards and best practices in Title 22, Division 12, Chapter 1 of the California Code of Regulations**, including:\n\n- **§101216** – Personnel Requirements\n- **§101216.1** – Teacher Qualifications\n- **§101216.2** – Teacher Aide Qualifications\n- **§101216.3** – Teacher-Child Ratios\n- **§101215.1** – Director Qualifications\n- **§101170** – Criminal Record Clearance\n- **Health and Safety Code §1596.866** – Pediatric CPR/First Aid Training\n\nThis means that:\n\n- All Yalla staff are at least 18 years old, have the physical and mental capacity to care for children, and are trained in areas such as health, safety and child development.\n- Caregivers meet or exceed the education and experience qualifications in §101216.1, and aides meet the criteria in §101216.2.\n- Caregiver-to-child ratios meet or exceed those required of licensed programs, ensuring appropriate supervision and individual care.\n- Yalla’s director holds the professional qualifications needed to oversee early childhood programs, consistent with §101215.1.\n- All staff and volunteers complete **criminal background clearance** in compliance with §101170.\n- At least one adult with current **pediatric CPR and First Aid certification** is always on site, per HSC §1596.866.\n\nYalla also **maintains the standard documentation** and internal records required in licensed settings, including staff health screenings, immunizations and mandated reporter training records.\n\nThe Parent/Caregiver understands that **not remaining on site** may result in the **immediate end of Flex care** and may **jeopardize the program’s lawful exemption status** under California Health and Safety Code §1596.792."}, {"id": "init-onsite", "type": "initials", "label": "I have read and agree to Section 10, including that I will remain on Yalla’s premises for the whole of every Flex session.", "required": true}, {"id": "s11", "type": "heading", "text": "11. Family Handbook"}, {"id": "s11-body", "type": "info", "text": "On behalf of themselves and the Child, the Parent/Caregiver agrees to follow Yalla’s policies, rules and regulations, as Yalla may update them, including those in the [Yalla Family Handbook](/portal/handbook), available in the Family Portal. By entering into this agreement, the Parent/Caregiver agrees to accept and abide by Yalla’s philosophy, rules, regulations, policies, procedures and standards expressed or implied in the Family Handbook or other written Yalla policies."}, {"id": "init-handbook", "type": "initials", "label": "I have read and agree to Section 11: Yalla’s Family Handbook and policies.", "required": true}, {"id": "s12", "type": "heading", "text": "12. Parental consent and indemnity"}, {"id": "s12-body", "type": "info", "text": "The Parent/Caregiver gives permission for the Child to take part in all Yalla programming, including developmentally appropriate experiences and daily caregiving. The Parent/Caregiver shall indemnify, defend, release and hold harmless Yalla from and against any and all claims, damages, expenses and other liabilities or injuries arising out of the Child’s participation in program activities, excluding only liabilities or injuries caused by the sole gross negligence of Yalla."}, {"id": "s13", "type": "heading", "text": "13. Force majeure"}, {"id": "s13-body", "type": "info", "text": "Yalla’s failure to perform under this agreement is excused to the extent it is caused, in whole or in part, by events beyond Yalla’s control, including without limitation acts of God, disease, epidemic, pandemic, quarantine, governmental actions, terrorism or threats of terrorism, fire, flood, earthquake, storm, explosion, lightning, power surges or failures, the elements, civil disturbances, strikes or labor disputes, failures of transportation facilities, or any similar unforeseen event that makes performance commercially impracticable, illegal or impossible (a “Force Majeure Event”).\n\nThe parties agree that if a Force Majeure Event occurs, Yalla is relieved from performance under this agreement whether or not the event was foreseeable when this agreement was signed. Within a reasonable time after a Force Majeure Event first occurs, Yalla will notify the Parent/Caregiver by email or other written correspondence. Yalla may suspend childcare and related activities, or take other measures in response, with as little as one hour’s notice, including ending the cohort year, as Yalla considers necessary."}, {"id": "s14", "type": "heading", "text": "14. Duty to report child abuse"}, {"id": "s14-body", "type": "info", "text": "Yalla staff are mandated reporters of suspected child abuse under California Penal Code §11166. Staff who, in their professional capacity or within the scope of their employment, know of or observe a child whom they know or reasonably suspect has been the victim of child abuse have a legal duty to report it to a child protective agency. Staff who know of or reasonably suspect that mental suffering has been inflicted on a child, or that a child’s emotional well-being is endangered in any other way, must also report it to a child protective agency."}, {"id": "s15", "type": "heading", "text": "15. Food"}, {"id": "s15-body", "type": "info", "text": "The Parent/Caregiver provides all food for the Child each day, following the guidelines in the [Yalla Family Handbook](/portal/handbook).\n\n- The Child must bring a nutritious, ready-to-eat lunch each day that follows Yalla’s dietary restrictions, choking-prevention requirements and safe food preparation policies. Food must be fully prepared in advance, stored with ice packs or in a thermos, and cut into safe, age-appropriate portions.\n- Yalla does not prepare or modify meals on site; each cohort space has a microwave for **optional meal reheating**, and the Parent/Caregiver may tell the Child’s caregiver whether they would like meals reheated.\n- Yalla provides snacks to children who eat solid foods.\n\nIf the Child arrives without enough food, or with food that does not follow Yalla’s safety or allergy guidelines, Yalla may ask the Parent/Caregiver to provide appropriate food. If food is missing or unsuitable and it is not resolved promptly, the Child may be sent home for the day. The Parent/Caregiver is responsible for making sure the Child’s food meets all safety, allergy and developmental requirements, to protect the health and well-being of every child in care. Yalla is a nut-free environment."}, {"id": "s16", "type": "heading", "text": "16. Non-discrimination"}, {"id": "s16-body", "type": "info", "text": "At Yalla Coworking & Childcare, we are deeply committed to a welcoming, inclusive and respectful environment for every family. We embrace children and caregivers of every race, ethnicity, national origin, family structure, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion and background.\n\nWe do not tolerate discrimination of any kind within our community, and all families are expected to uphold these values. Discriminatory behavior, or conduct that undermines the inclusive nature of our program, may result in the end of Flex care under Section 6. We believe diversity strengthens our community, and we are proud to welcome families of all kinds."}, {"id": "s17", "type": "heading", "text": "17. Waiver"}, {"id": "s17-body", "type": "info", "text": "No right under this agreement is waived (lost) merely by delaying or failing to exercise it. Consent to one act is not consent to any other or later act. Any waiver of a default under this agreement must be in writing and is not a waiver of any other default concerning the same or any other provision of this agreement."}, {"id": "s18", "type": "heading", "text": "18. Good faith"}, {"id": "s18-body", "type": "info", "text": "At Yalla, we believe in a partnership built on mutual trust and respect. Yalla and the Parent/Caregiver each agree to act in good faith and with mutual respect for the duration of this agreement, including:\n\n- **Honesty and transparency:** communicating honestly and openly about all matters related to the Child’s care, health and well-being.\n- **Timely communication:** sharing any concerns, issues or changes in circumstances that may affect the Child’s care promptly, so they can be resolved quickly with minimal disruption.\n- **Respectful interactions:** conducting all interactions between Yalla, the Parent/Caregiver and other members of the Yalla community with mutual respect and consideration.\n- **Cooperation and collaboration:** working together to address any issues or challenges, seeking solutions in the best interest of the Child.\n- **Commitment to these terms:** following the terms of this agreement, understanding that its success depends on the reliability and integrity of both Yalla and the Parent/Caregiver.\n\nBy signing, both parties commit to acting in good faith to support a positive environment for the Child’s growth and development."}, {"id": "s19", "type": "heading", "text": "19. Governing law"}, {"id": "s19-body", "type": "info", "text": "This agreement is governed by the laws of the State of California, without regard to conflict-of-laws principles. Each party irrevocably consents to the exclusive personal jurisdiction and venue of the federal and state courts located in the County of San Diego, California, for any matter arising out of or relating to this agreement."}, {"id": "sign", "type": "heading", "text": "Signatures"}, {"id": "sign-body", "type": "info", "text": "**The undersigned have read and understand this agreement.**\n\nThis agreement and the [Yalla Family Handbook](/portal/handbook) (available in the Family Portal) set out all of Yalla’s obligations; there are no other implied obligations. Any changes to this agreement must be in writing and signed by both parties.\n\nYalla accepts this agreement on the date it is signed below. Accepted for Yalla Childcare LLC by Elizabeth Coburn, Managing Partner."}, {"id": "read-understood", "type": "agree", "label": "I am the child’s parent or legal guardian and have read and agree to the Sprouts Flex admission agreement. This agreement applies to any Sprouts Flex sessions I book and does not require a commitment to future care. A new agreement is required only when my child moves to another Flex cohort or one year after signing, whichever comes first.", "required": true}, {"id": "signature", "type": "signature", "label": "Parent/Caregiver signature"}]'::jsonb, "content_hash" = '6ca50394e766bb26da1efa90478858a3a7f94d88ef9dece408db0a1d28700482' WHERE "id" = 'flex-agreement-sprouts-v1' AND "body" = 'Please read this agreement carefully. Add your initials where asked, then print your name and sign at the end. Once signed, it stays on file for one year, so you won’t be asked to sign it again before then.' AND "fields"::text LIKE '%Yalla’s [Illness Policy](/portal/illness-policy), available in the Family Portal%' AND "fields"::text NOT LIKE '%(/portal/handbook%' AND NOT "fields" @> '[{"id": "parent-name"}]'::jsonb;
--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE "form_versions" SET "body" = 'Please read this agreement carefully. Add your initials where asked, then print your name and sign at the end. Once signed, it stays on file for one year, so you won’t be asked to sign it again before then.', "fields" = '[{"id": "intro", "type": "info", "text": "**Yalla Flex Admission Agreement · Wildflowers (3 – 4 years) · 2026–2027**\n\nThis agreement is between Yalla Childcare LLC, doing business as Yalla Coworking & Childcare (“Yalla”), and the parent or caregiver signing below (the “Parent/Caregiver”), for the child named on this agreement (the “Child”). It covers every Yalla Flex session the Child attends for one (1) year from the date it is signed (the “Effective Date”). A new agreement must be signed before booking further Flex sessions when the Child moves to another Flex cohort or one year after signing, whichever comes first.\n\nThis agreement is a binding contract enforceable under the laws of the State of California. By signing, the Parent/Caregiver confirms they have read and accept these terms."}, {"id": "s1", "type": "heading", "text": "1. Overview"}, {"id": "s1-body", "type": "info", "text": "Yalla Coworking & Childcare is a license-exempt early childhood program operated at **408 Nutmeg Street, San Diego, CA 92103**, in accordance with California Health and Safety Code §1596.792. Yalla is directed and managed by a team of qualified administrators and early childhood educators committed to high-quality, developmentally appropriate care and enrichment for young children. The program supports children’s social, emotional, cognitive and physical development through play, inquiry-based learning and nurturing supervision.\n\nThis agreement applies to **Yalla Flex**, which lets children attend on an as-needed basis, without a recurring weekly or monthly schedule, when a spot is open in their age group. In this agreement, “childcare” means non-medical supervision and early learning experiences provided while the Child is on site."}, {"id": "s2", "type": "heading", "text": "2. Program hours and booking"}, {"id": "s2-body", "type": "info", "text": "Yalla Flex is available Monday through Friday, subject to availability:\n\n- **Full day:** 8:30 AM – 4:30 PM\n- **Half day:** 8:30 AM – 12:00 PM\n\nFlex sessions are booked online through the Yalla website or the Family Portal. A spot is available only when there is an opening in the Child’s age group; open days are shown on the booking calendar. Because our cohorts need time to prepare for each child, booking for a given day closes at 8:00 AM that morning. Yalla is closed, and Flex is not available, on the closure days listed on Yalla’s cohort year calendar.\n\nEarly Bird care is offered from 8:00–8:30 AM for children 12 months and older, at $16 per day, on days when Yalla has Early Bird space available. Early Bird space is limited and is shown at booking when it is available; an open Flex session does not guarantee an Early Bird space."}, {"id": "s3", "type": "heading", "text": "3. Rates, reservations and payment"}, {"id": "s3-body", "type": "info", "text": "**Wildflowers (3 – 4 years) Flex rates**\n\n- **Full day (8:30 AM – 4:30 PM):** $150 per day\n- **Half day (8:30 AM – 12:00 PM):** $75 per day\n\nFlex rates include access to Yalla’s coworking space and amenities for the Parent/Caregiver, and snacks (for children eating solid foods), materials and participation in all programming offered during the Child’s booked hours. When siblings attend the same program on the same day, each additional child receives a 10% sibling discount, applied automatically at checkout.\n\nAll Flex sessions must be booked in advance and are paid in full at the time of booking. A session is reserved for the Child once payment is complete. The Parent/Caregiver may book one day at a time or several days at once; dates that have not been booked and paid for are not held, and availability may change.\n\nPrior use of Flex does not secure or prioritize future availability. Priority for cohort spaces is always given to Club Yalla members."}, {"id": "init-rates", "type": "initials", "label": "I have read and agree to Section 3: Flex rates, reservations and payment.", "required": true}, {"id": "s4", "type": "heading", "text": "4. Cancellations, absences and credits"}, {"id": "s4-body", "type": "info", "text": "When the Parent/Caregiver cancels a Flex session at least 24 hours before it begins, the amount paid is returned to the family’s Yalla Wallet as a credit. Credits can be used toward future Yalla bookings for up to 24 months from the date they are issued, have no cash value and are not refunded or transferred, except where required by law. Cancellations made less than 24 hours before a session, and no-shows, are not eligible for credit.\n\nIllness and other extenuating circumstances may be exempt from the 24-hour requirement; please contact Yalla as soon as possible. Cancel through the Family Portal, call 619.775.4008 or email hello@yallaspacesd.com.\n\nRepeated no-shows or cancellations without timely communication may result in the temporary suspension of Flex booking."}, {"id": "s5", "type": "heading", "text": "5. Child illness policy"}, {"id": "s5-body", "type": "info", "text": "The Parent/Caregiver agrees to follow Yalla’s [Illness Policy](/portal/illness-policy), available in the Family Portal. If the Child shows signs or symptoms of illness described in the policy, the Child will be separated from the group and supervised by Yalla staff until the Parent/Caregiver or another authorized adult collects the Child.\n\nThe Child will also be sent home when Yalla believes, in its sole judgment, that the Child’s condition poses a threat to the health or safety of the Child, other children or staff. Because the Parent/Caregiver remains on site during Flex sessions, **the Parent/Caregiver must collect the Child within twenty (20) minutes of being notified of the Child’s illness.** After twenty minutes, the Parent/Caregiver will be charged the actual cost of any additional expenses related to isolated care.\n\nIf the Child is sent home because of illness, the rest of that session is treated as an absence under Section 4.\n\nThe Child should be symptom-free for 24 hours before returning to care. Knowingly bringing a sick child to Yalla is a serious matter; repeated instances may result in the permanent end of Flex booking as described in Section 6. By signing this agreement, the Parent/Caregiver accepts responsibility for following the Illness Policy to protect the health and safety of all children in the program."}, {"id": "s6", "type": "heading", "text": "6. Ending Flex care"}, {"id": "s6-body", "type": "info", "text": "Yalla may end the Child’s participation in Yalla Flex **effective immediately** if any of the following occur:\n\n- In the sole discretion of Yalla’s leadership team, the behavior of the Child or the Parent/Caregiver presents a significant risk to the physical or emotional well-being of Yalla staff or anyone else on the premises, and that risk cannot be reasonably resolved through restorative communication.\n- Any amount owed to Yalla (for example, a late departure fee) is not paid within 10 days after it is due.\n- The Child is collected late more than three times in any thirty-day period without advance notice to Yalla.\n- The Child’s immunization record is not brought into compliance with California’s childcare immunization requirements within 21 days of the due date.\n\n*In compliance with California Health and Safety Code Sections 120325–120375, any child attending a private or public elementary or secondary school, childcare or preschool facility, day nursery, nursery school, family day care home or development center in California must be fully immunized before entry. Childcare providers are required to enforce immunization requirements, maintain immunization records and submit reports.*\n\n**Yalla also reserves the right to suspend or permanently end Flex booking at any time for any of the following reasons:**\n\n- Repeated failure to follow Yalla’s policies\n- Non-payment or repeated late payment of amounts owed\n- Behavior deemed unsafe or harmful by Yalla’s leadership\n- Repeated late departures\n- Missing required immunization documentation\n\nThese decisions are made at Yalla’s sole discretion to preserve the safety and integrity of the program."}, {"id": "s7", "type": "heading", "text": "7. Availability"}, {"id": "s7-body", "type": "info", "text": "Flex care can be booked at any time during the cohort year; however, availability is not guaranteed. Many of our cohorts are at or near capacity, and Flex is available only when there is an opening in the Child’s age group. Signing this agreement does not guarantee space on any particular day."}, {"id": "s8", "type": "heading", "text": "8. Arrival, departure and releasing children"}, {"id": "s8-body", "type": "info", "text": "Yalla will release the Child only to:\n\n- The Parent/Caregiver\n- An adult the Parent/Caregiver has authorized in writing in advance, listed in the family’s profile; or\n- Police or child welfare workers with proper authorization.\n\n**Yalla will never release the Child to anyone under the age of 18.**\n\nThe Parent/Caregiver or an authorized adult must check the Child in and sign the Child out at Yalla’s lobby kiosk at arrival and departure **every day**. The Child may never be taken from Yalla without first notifying the leadership team or the lead educarer or guide on duty in the Child’s cohort. Anyone other than the Parent/Caregiver who collects the Child must show a driver’s license or other valid photo identification.\n\nPlease plan to collect the Child by the end of the booked session. After a five-minute grace period, a late departure fee of $10 is charged for each additional ten minutes, or portion of ten minutes."}, {"id": "s9", "type": "heading", "text": "9. Educarers, guides and substitute care"}, {"id": "s9-body", "type": "info", "text": "The Child’s lead and supporting educarers and guides provide the vast majority of care and set the daily rhythm for the group. All caregivers are CPR and First Aid certified and have completed a LiveScan background check. Under Yalla’s own program requirements, caregivers also hold relevant advanced degrees and certifications.\n\nThere will be times when a cohort’s primary caregivers are attending professional development, out sick or away for personal matters. When the lead caregiver is absent, a supporting caregiver steps in as lead. A highly qualified substitute who spends time with the children at least once a month is available if both the lead and supporting caregivers are absent, so the program does not have to close.\n\nYalla is committed to hiring supporting caregivers and substitutes who are highly qualified and compensated well above industry standards for these roles. The Parent/Caregiver will be told of any change to the normal daily rhythm, including a change in the primary caregiver.\n\nAdult-to-child ratios are maintained throughout each program day at no more than 1:4 for children under 20 months, 1:6 for children 20 to 35 months, and 1:8 for children 3 years and older. The Wildflowers cohort (3 – 4 years) is cared for at a ratio of no more than 1:8."}, {"id": "s10", "type": "heading", "text": "10. Staff qualifications, legal exemption status and onsite parent requirement"}, {"id": "s10-body", "type": "info", "text": "The Parent/Caregiver acknowledges that **Yalla is a license-exempt program** operating in accordance with **California Health and Safety Code §1596.792**. As a condition of this exemption, the Parent/Caregiver agrees to **remain physically present on Yalla’s premises at all times during the Child’s Flex session**. This exemption depends on the Child’s parent or legal guardian being on site and immediately available to provide care if needed, as defined by California law.\n\nYalla is deeply committed to the safety, development and well-being of every child, and **voluntarily follows the staff qualifications, safety standards and best practices in Title 22, Division 12, Chapter 1 of the California Code of Regulations**, including:\n\n- **§101216** – Personnel Requirements\n- **§101216.1** – Teacher Qualifications\n- **§101216.2** – Teacher Aide Qualifications\n- **§101216.3** – Teacher-Child Ratios\n- **§101215.1** – Director Qualifications\n- **§101170** – Criminal Record Clearance\n- **Health and Safety Code §1596.866** – Pediatric CPR/First Aid Training\n\nThis means that:\n\n- All Yalla staff are at least 18 years old, have the physical and mental capacity to care for children, and are trained in areas such as health, safety and child development.\n- Caregivers meet or exceed the education and experience qualifications in §101216.1, and aides meet the criteria in §101216.2.\n- Caregiver-to-child ratios meet or exceed those required of licensed programs, ensuring appropriate supervision and individual care.\n- Yalla’s director holds the professional qualifications needed to oversee early childhood programs, consistent with §101215.1.\n- All staff and volunteers complete **criminal background clearance** in compliance with §101170.\n- At least one adult with current **pediatric CPR and First Aid certification** is always on site, per HSC §1596.866.\n\nYalla also **maintains the standard documentation** and internal records required in licensed settings, including staff health screenings, immunizations and mandated reporter training records.\n\nThe Parent/Caregiver understands that **not remaining on site** may result in the **immediate end of Flex care** and may **jeopardize the program’s lawful exemption status** under California Health and Safety Code §1596.792."}, {"id": "init-onsite", "type": "initials", "label": "I have read and agree to Section 10, including that I will remain on Yalla’s premises for the whole of every Flex session.", "required": true}, {"id": "s11", "type": "heading", "text": "11. Family Handbook"}, {"id": "s11-body", "type": "info", "text": "On behalf of themselves and the Child, the Parent/Caregiver agrees to follow Yalla’s policies, rules and regulations, as Yalla may update them, including those in the [Yalla Family Handbook](/portal/handbook), available in the Family Portal. By entering into this agreement, the Parent/Caregiver agrees to accept and abide by Yalla’s philosophy, rules, regulations, policies, procedures and standards expressed or implied in the Family Handbook or other written Yalla policies."}, {"id": "init-handbook", "type": "initials", "label": "I have read and agree to Section 11: Yalla’s Family Handbook and policies.", "required": true}, {"id": "s12", "type": "heading", "text": "12. Parental consent and indemnity"}, {"id": "s12-body", "type": "info", "text": "The Parent/Caregiver gives permission for the Child to take part in all Yalla programming, including developmentally appropriate experiences and daily caregiving. The Parent/Caregiver shall indemnify, defend, release and hold harmless Yalla from and against any and all claims, damages, expenses and other liabilities or injuries arising out of the Child’s participation in program activities, excluding only liabilities or injuries caused by the sole gross negligence of Yalla."}, {"id": "s13", "type": "heading", "text": "13. Force majeure"}, {"id": "s13-body", "type": "info", "text": "Yalla’s failure to perform under this agreement is excused to the extent it is caused, in whole or in part, by events beyond Yalla’s control, including without limitation acts of God, disease, epidemic, pandemic, quarantine, governmental actions, terrorism or threats of terrorism, fire, flood, earthquake, storm, explosion, lightning, power surges or failures, the elements, civil disturbances, strikes or labor disputes, failures of transportation facilities, or any similar unforeseen event that makes performance commercially impracticable, illegal or impossible (a “Force Majeure Event”).\n\nThe parties agree that if a Force Majeure Event occurs, Yalla is relieved from performance under this agreement whether or not the event was foreseeable when this agreement was signed. Within a reasonable time after a Force Majeure Event first occurs, Yalla will notify the Parent/Caregiver by email or other written correspondence. Yalla may suspend childcare and related activities, or take other measures in response, with as little as one hour’s notice, including ending the cohort year, as Yalla considers necessary."}, {"id": "s14", "type": "heading", "text": "14. Duty to report child abuse"}, {"id": "s14-body", "type": "info", "text": "Yalla staff are mandated reporters of suspected child abuse under California Penal Code §11166. Staff who, in their professional capacity or within the scope of their employment, know of or observe a child whom they know or reasonably suspect has been the victim of child abuse have a legal duty to report it to a child protective agency. Staff who know of or reasonably suspect that mental suffering has been inflicted on a child, or that a child’s emotional well-being is endangered in any other way, must also report it to a child protective agency."}, {"id": "s15", "type": "heading", "text": "15. Food"}, {"id": "s15-body", "type": "info", "text": "The Parent/Caregiver provides all food for the Child each day, following the guidelines in the [Yalla Family Handbook](/portal/handbook).\n\n- The Child must bring a nutritious, ready-to-eat lunch each day that follows Yalla’s dietary restrictions, choking-prevention requirements and safe food preparation policies. Food must be fully prepared in advance, stored with ice packs or in a thermos, and cut into safe, age-appropriate portions.\n- Yalla does not prepare or modify meals on site; each cohort space has a microwave for **optional meal reheating**, and the Parent/Caregiver may tell the Child’s caregiver whether they would like meals reheated.\n- Yalla provides snacks to children who eat solid foods.\n\nIf the Child arrives without enough food, or with food that does not follow Yalla’s safety or allergy guidelines, Yalla may ask the Parent/Caregiver to provide appropriate food. If food is missing or unsuitable and it is not resolved promptly, the Child may be sent home for the day. The Parent/Caregiver is responsible for making sure the Child’s food meets all safety, allergy and developmental requirements, to protect the health and well-being of every child in care. Yalla is a nut-free environment."}, {"id": "s16", "type": "heading", "text": "16. Non-discrimination"}, {"id": "s16-body", "type": "info", "text": "At Yalla Coworking & Childcare, we are deeply committed to a welcoming, inclusive and respectful environment for every family. We embrace children and caregivers of every race, ethnicity, national origin, family structure, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion and background.\n\nWe do not tolerate discrimination of any kind within our community, and all families are expected to uphold these values. Discriminatory behavior, or conduct that undermines the inclusive nature of our program, may result in the end of Flex care under Section 6. We believe diversity strengthens our community, and we are proud to welcome families of all kinds."}, {"id": "s17", "type": "heading", "text": "17. Waiver"}, {"id": "s17-body", "type": "info", "text": "No right under this agreement is waived (lost) merely by delaying or failing to exercise it. Consent to one act is not consent to any other or later act. Any waiver of a default under this agreement must be in writing and is not a waiver of any other default concerning the same or any other provision of this agreement."}, {"id": "s18", "type": "heading", "text": "18. Good faith"}, {"id": "s18-body", "type": "info", "text": "At Yalla, we believe in a partnership built on mutual trust and respect. Yalla and the Parent/Caregiver each agree to act in good faith and with mutual respect for the duration of this agreement, including:\n\n- **Honesty and transparency:** communicating honestly and openly about all matters related to the Child’s care, health and well-being.\n- **Timely communication:** sharing any concerns, issues or changes in circumstances that may affect the Child’s care promptly, so they can be resolved quickly with minimal disruption.\n- **Respectful interactions:** conducting all interactions between Yalla, the Parent/Caregiver and other members of the Yalla community with mutual respect and consideration.\n- **Cooperation and collaboration:** working together to address any issues or challenges, seeking solutions in the best interest of the Child.\n- **Commitment to these terms:** following the terms of this agreement, understanding that its success depends on the reliability and integrity of both Yalla and the Parent/Caregiver.\n\nBy signing, both parties commit to acting in good faith to support a positive environment for the Child’s growth and development."}, {"id": "s19", "type": "heading", "text": "19. Governing law"}, {"id": "s19-body", "type": "info", "text": "This agreement is governed by the laws of the State of California, without regard to conflict-of-laws principles. Each party irrevocably consents to the exclusive personal jurisdiction and venue of the federal and state courts located in the County of San Diego, California, for any matter arising out of or relating to this agreement."}, {"id": "sign", "type": "heading", "text": "Signatures"}, {"id": "sign-body", "type": "info", "text": "**The undersigned have read and understand this agreement.**\n\nThis agreement and the [Yalla Family Handbook](/portal/handbook) (available in the Family Portal) set out all of Yalla’s obligations; there are no other implied obligations. Any changes to this agreement must be in writing and signed by both parties.\n\nYalla accepts this agreement on the date it is signed below. Accepted for Yalla Childcare LLC by Elizabeth Coburn, Managing Partner."}, {"id": "read-understood", "type": "agree", "label": "I am the child’s parent or legal guardian and have read and agree to the Wildflowers Flex admission agreement. This agreement applies to any Wildflowers Flex sessions I book and does not require a commitment to future care. A new agreement is required only when my child moves to another Flex cohort or one year after signing, whichever comes first.", "required": true}, {"id": "signature", "type": "signature", "label": "Parent/Caregiver signature"}]'::jsonb, "content_hash" = '469c506560aa4e8e47e1afa748ab140f005b84025901e6afca83f428c6b7dddd' WHERE "id" = 'flex-agreement-wildflowers-v1' AND "body" = 'Please read this agreement carefully. Add your initials where asked, then print your name and sign at the end. Once signed, it stays on file for one year, so you won’t be asked to sign it again before then.' AND "fields"::text LIKE '%Yalla’s [Illness Policy](/portal/illness-policy), available in the Family Portal%' AND "fields"::text NOT LIKE '%(/portal/handbook%' AND NOT "fields" @> '[{"id": "parent-name"}]'::jsonb;
